# Env for the API test run (JEF-656). Copy to apps/api/.env.test (gitignored):
#
#   cp .env.test.example .env.test
#
# `pnpm setup:worktree` does this for a new worktree, and CI's `test` job does it
# before `pnpm test`, so a local run and CI read the same file.
#
# It holds no values on purpose. CI's test job has never had an env file, and the
# suite is written to pass with an empty environment: a test that needs a value
# sets it itself. What this file does is stop apps/api/.env, the dev server's
# file, being loaded instead (src/__tests__/setupEnv.ts reads .env.test when it
# exists and .env otherwise). That file sets PLANS_ENFORCED=true,
# BILLING_PROVIDER=polar and an absolute API_ORIGIN, which makes seven
# integration tests fail locally (billingWebhook, mcp, shareLinks).
#
# A variable exported in the shell still wins over anything here. Add a line only
# when a test cannot set the value itself, and add it here, not in ci.yml.
